                <pb facs="1001" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2963: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-09T17:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. Your 211, December 7, 3 p.m. Has the mission hospital at Dessie been
                    incorporated into the Ethiopian Red Cross or into the sanitary formations of the
                    Ethiopian Army, or is it functioning merely as an independent American
                    institution? In the latter case it presumably had no right to the use of the Red
                    Cross emblem under the Red Cross Convention signed at Geneva on July 27,
                    1929.</p>
                <p>According to the Department’s records American missionaries now maintain the
                    following hospitals or clinics in Ethiopia: three at Addis Ababa and one at each
                    of the following places: Gore, Sayo, <pb facs="1002" n="900" xml:id="pg900"/>
                    Soddu, Dessie and Debra Tabor. Please confirm this information and indicate
                    which, if any, of these institutions have become affiliated with Ethiopian Red
                    Cross or Ethiopian Army sanitary formations and which continue to function as
                    purely American units.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
